# Drafted by Gemini (R17 workbench), edited.

~ bench
if not flag.mr_antidote_known
Narrator: Glass retorts and brass burners sit cold in the violet hum. Without a proper formula in hand, all these vials are only guesswork.
-> END
endif
Narrator: You lay your gathered vials beside the copper still: pale mnemonic residue, bitter noetic extract, and jars of cold unrefined ichor measured out for the work.
* [if flag.mnemonic_residue >= 1 and flag.noetic_extract >= 1 and flag.unrefined_ichor >= 1] Brew one dose (ten minutes) -> brew
* Leave -> END

~ brew
Narrator: The spirit lamp catches with a low blue hiss, warming the heavy glass coil.
* [Arcana DC 18] Brew with arcane knowledge -> brew_ok | brew_fail
* [Intelligence DC 13] Brew with Alchemist's Supplies -> brew_ok | brew_fail
* Step back from the burner -> bench

~ brew_ok
Narrator: The cloudy ichor turns clear as rain and settles into a single warm, amber draught that smells faintly of bruised sage.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at that clarity. A triumph of proper calibration over cellar filth.
set mnemonic_residue -= 1
set noetic_extract -= 1
set unrefined_ichor -= 1
set lethic_antidote_doses += 1
set mr_cure_found
quest the_lethic_antidote brewed
-> bench

~ brew_fail
Narrator: The mixture curdles into grey foam and scorches the flask, spoiling the measure of raw ichor before you can cool the glass.
set unrefined_ichor -= 1
-> bench

~ triage
Narrator: The quiet wards smell of rain and old linen now. You hold fewer stoppered doses in your palm than there are blank eyes waiting in the halls.
* [if flag.lethic_antidote_doses >= 1 and not flag.amos_cousin_cured] Give a dose to Catherine -> triage_catherine
* [if flag.lethic_antidote_doses >= 1] Give a dose to the patients first -> triage_patients
* [if flag.lethic_antidote_doses >= 1] Give a dose to a mutant orderly -> triage_orderly
* Morgan's slow cure will reach the rest -> triage_done

~ triage_catherine
approve rook_coldwake +3 tobin_hayward +2: You gave a dose of the antidote to restore Catherine first
Narrator: Catherine drinks the warm draught, shivers once, and looks down at her mended left arm as her true name comes rushing back.
catherine_winthrop [weary]: Tell Amos I am sorry for that foolish letter. Tell him I am coming home.
interject name:tobin_hayward: There now, girl. Pulse is steady and the rot is out.
set lethic_antidote_doses -= 1
set amos_cousin_cured
set mr_patients_cured += 1
-> triage

~ triage_patients
approve tobin_hayward +3 lucan_houndstooth +2: You spent your brewed antidote tending the helpless ward patients
Narrator: You tip a vial between a patient's parted lips; colour creeps back into grey cheeks, and a whispered name breaks the long silence of the ward.
set lethic_antidote_doses -= 1
set mr_patients_cured += 1
-> triage

~ triage_orderly
approve tobin_hayward +3 delphine_ravelle +2 cordelia_skein +2: You gave a dose of antidote to cure a twisted orderly
Narrator: The trembling orderly unfastens the porcelain mask and drinks; the twisted stiffness in the jaw loosens, and a pair of tired human eyes blinks up at you.
set lethic_antidote_doses -= 1
set mr_orderly_cured += 1
-> triage

~ triage_done
Narrator: You cork the empty case and leave the rest to time, warm broth, and the slower remedies coming from Wickermoor.
-> END
